In other words, all of this is required to enable us to be able to operate more and more fruitfully in the divine will.

209
00:21:26.140 --> 00:21:45.140
Because when we started out on this journey, we weren't really talking all this practicality, were we? Because we had to sort of grasp something of what was being said, so I don't talk practicality until I feel that people are really able for it.

210
00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:48.140
And you don't force them to do something ahead of time.

211
00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:57.140
Just like with children, you begin with ABC. You don't begin with trigonometry.

212
00:21:57.140 --> 00:22:10.140
So every single thing that Jesus has said to her is some aspect of drawing us to come to be able to operate the divine will effectively.

213
00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:22.140
So each effect I speak to you about contains its own distinct property. Therefore, by not manifesting all the goods which are in my will and where the soul can reach.

214
00:22:22.140 --> 00:22:27.140
Now that's what he was talking about in the last message, where the soul can reach.

215
00:22:27.140 --> 00:22:42.140
Because as Catholics and ordinary believers, all we know is that you say your rosary or you do your novina or whatever, and your hope for a response.

216
00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:54.140
This belongs to a different world altogether, where in a very small movement of your soul, you're affecting all humanity, past, present and future.

217
00:22:54.140 --> 00:23:03.140
So people living on the ordinary level of spirituality wouldn't know what you were getting at at all.

218
00:23:03.140 --> 00:23:18.140
I tried that out with a fervent Christian who visited me and I just made a prayer in the car when we were driving along and she said to me, that's funny, praying.

219
00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:28.140
Never heard praying like that before. What are you getting at? Because she was expecting the ordinary. This is not the ordinary.

220
00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:37.140
And I said, I'm just sowing a seed. And if I can create curiosity in you, I won't respond to it now, but come back.

221
00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:43.140
I just left it with her. I said, this is what the Lord's teaching us now.

222
00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:51.140
And she said, I've never heard anybody ever pray like that before. And I said, let's grant just sowing a seed.

223
00:23:51.140 --> 00:24:04.140
So where the soul can reach, in other words, entering into the divine will gives the soul real power to do things for souls and for God.

224
00:24:04.140 --> 00:24:12.140
But you have to be actually living in the divine will, not just saying prayers.

225
00:24:12.140 --> 00:24:32.140
So they show where the soul can reach by living in the divine will, and you would cause either a bait in order to capture them, which is what I was doing by saying that prayer, or a taste to attract them or a magnet to draw them, or a food to satiate them to be missing.

226
00:24:32.140 --> 00:24:38.140
In other words, a grace that God had intended for them to receive wouldn't be received.

227
00:24:38.140 --> 00:24:49.140
So the perfect harmony, the pleasure of the fragrances, the light to guide them would be lacking, and not finding all possible goods, that is not knowing them.

228
00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:55.140
They would not have the great yearnings to rise above all other things.

229
00:24:55.140 --> 00:25:06.140
Now, that's what's been happening to us as we've journeyed through these volumes, that the desire to move in this direction becomes greater and greater.

230
00:25:06.140 --> 00:25:10.140
The desire to pray like this becomes greater and greater.

231
00:25:10.140 --> 00:25:17.140
The desire to understand it more becomes greater and greater, and that's what gets you on your feet.

232
00:25:17.140 --> 00:25:24.140
And that's why he talks about the necessity of the knowledge that we need to understand it.

233
00:25:24.140 --> 00:25:32.140
So if they don't know them, they wouldn't have the great yearning to rise above all things in order to live in the divine will.

234
00:25:32.140 --> 00:25:39.140
Okay, so, and besides, do not worry about what you were told.

235
00:25:39.140 --> 00:25:48.140
My mother also contained my will as life, and yet the world continued in its course of evil.

236
00:25:48.140 --> 00:25:56.140
While we reach out to all souls, not all souls will be reached, simply because some are closed off, some are dead.

237
00:25:56.140 --> 00:26:03.140
Okay, and so at any particular moment, it's according to the disposition of souls.

238
00:26:03.140 --> 00:26:10.140
Okay, and in nothing did it appear to be changed.

239
00:26:10.140 --> 00:26:20.140
It's the really color of the word appear, because during the lifetime of our blessed mother, someone could have said to her,

240
00:26:20.140 --> 00:26:25.140
"What use is it to the rest of us that you are born immaculate?"

241
00:26:25.140 --> 00:26:30.140
All you're doing is you're living in that little house by yourself, you're minding your own little kitchen garden,

242
00:26:30.140 --> 00:26:35.140
you're minding your own little house, and you're looking after your own little son of what use is that to us.

243
00:26:35.140 --> 00:26:42.140
You see, externally, it didn't appear, and yet you changed all history.

244
00:26:42.140 --> 00:26:49.140
So externally, it might not appear to us either that anything is happening, and yet it is.

245
00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:51.140
Is that okay?

246
00:26:51.140 --> 00:27:06.140
Not one external miracle came from her, and yet what she did not do in the low world that's on the earth, she did in heaven with her creator.

247
00:27:06.140 --> 00:27:13.140
By her continuous living in the divine will, she formed the place within herself.

248
00:27:13.140 --> 00:27:23.140
Now notice the space that you enter into this space, and it's this space, this world within us that we have to give God.

249
00:27:23.140 --> 00:27:31.140
I spoke about that at Mary's Hill, that we've got to give God this space to work in this void.

250
00:27:31.140 --> 00:27:41.140
Okay, so she formed the space within herself in order to draw the word to become incarnate upon the earth.

251
00:27:41.140 --> 00:27:45.140
So she changed the destiny of mankind.

252
00:27:45.140 --> 00:27:53.140
So externally, her neighbors couldn't see any difference between her and everybody else, she was just a very nice lady.

253
00:27:53.140 --> 00:27:58.140
Okay, internally, everything was different.

254
00:27:58.140 --> 00:28:05.140
So we have to understand that as far as the world is concerned, and even the people you're living with,

255
00:28:05.140 --> 00:28:14.140
they might call you a nice lady, or a nice gentleman, but they won't understand at all what God is doing with you, and that's actually your safety.

256
00:28:14.140 --> 00:28:16.140
That's actually your safety.

257
00:28:16.140 --> 00:28:19.140
But she changed the destiny of mankind.

258
00:28:19.140 --> 00:28:26.140
She performed the greatest of miracles which no one else had done or ever will do.

259
00:28:26.140 --> 00:28:34.140
She had a unique miracle, and it was to transport heaven upon the earth.

260
00:28:34.140 --> 00:28:36.140
Isn't that fantastic?

261
00:28:36.140 --> 00:28:45.140
So she was to bring heaven down to the earth to the point where the second person of the Blessed Trinity actually became man on the earth.

262
00:28:45.140 --> 00:28:50.140
For one who must do the greatest things, it's not necessary to do the lesser.

263
00:28:50.140 --> 00:28:56.140
Now, I think you should put VIP about 10 feet high on the one.

264
00:28:56.140 --> 00:29:09.140
Why? Because we're inclined to stay with the lesser things that we know and we're familiar with, instead of leaving the lesser things behind us and going only further greater.

265
00:29:09.140 --> 00:29:12.140
Well, we find that very difficult.

266
00:29:12.140 --> 00:29:16.140
In life, there is good, better, and best.

267
00:29:16.140 --> 00:29:23.140
Now, the enemy of the good is the better, or the enemy of the better is the good, I should say.

268
00:29:23.140 --> 00:29:26.140
I said it backways, didn't I?

269
00:29:26.140 --> 00:29:34.140
Because a person who is at the stage of the good won't want to let that go because I am better than other people.

270
00:29:34.140 --> 00:29:38.140
And so they may refuse to go on to the next stage.

271
00:29:38.140 --> 00:29:49.140
Now, but if they let the good go and receive the better, they're in a much higher place and can affect the human race very much more.

272
00:29:49.140 --> 00:29:53.140
And so John of the Cross is very strong on this one.

273
00:29:53.140 --> 00:29:58.140
The enemy of the best is the better.

274
00:29:58.140 --> 00:30:03.140
We find it even harder to let go the better for the best.

275
00:30:03.140 --> 00:30:09.140
And so John of the Cross says that, and I'm giving it to you in my words now.

276
00:30:09.140 --> 00:30:11.140
I'm not giving it to you as an actual quotation.

277
00:30:11.140 --> 00:30:20.140
John of the Cross says that some people stop about five yards from the goal of union with God.

278
00:30:20.140 --> 00:30:26.140
They just won't take the best because they have the better.

279
00:30:26.140 --> 00:30:34.140
So that's why you have this very strong thing in St. Therese of Lissure that we go to God with empty hands.

280
00:30:34.140 --> 00:30:38.140
We're not clinging to what I was.

281
00:30:38.140 --> 00:30:42.140
I love that statement in that film, Ebenezer Scrooge.

282
00:30:42.140 --> 00:30:44.140
I'm not the man I was.

283
00:30:44.140 --> 00:30:48.140
And I think we should be able to say that on a daily basis.

284
00:30:48.140 --> 00:30:50.140
I'm not the person I was.

285
00:30:50.140 --> 00:30:52.140
I'm actually in a different place.

286
00:30:52.140 --> 00:30:54.140
And I'm going forward.

287
00:30:54.140 --> 00:30:58.140
And I'm going to continue to go forward no matter where it takes me.

288
00:30:58.140 --> 00:31:01.140
I'm going to let the past go.

289
00:31:01.140 --> 00:31:07.140
And we should be able to actually look back and say, I am not actually the person I was last year.

290
00:31:07.140 --> 00:31:08.140
I've moved.

291
00:31:08.140 --> 00:31:12.140
Now nobody else might notice except the Lord and yourself.

292
00:31:12.140 --> 00:31:16.140
And so we have to be very careful.

293
00:31:16.140 --> 00:31:22.140
An example I would give you and I hope I won't walk on people's corners because examples can be dangerous.

294
00:31:22.140 --> 00:31:28.140
And that is that many people have come into the divine will through the charismatic renewal.

295
00:31:28.140 --> 00:31:35.140
The charismatic renewal was absolutely fantastic for getting people to know the Lord personally.

296
00:31:35.140 --> 00:31:41.140
Getting repentance into their lives, getting conversion into their lives, reading scripture every day,

297
00:31:41.140 --> 00:31:49.140
getting them into adoration and therefore getting them into a way of life that would actually prepare them to move on.

298
00:31:49.140 --> 00:31:51.140
Some of them can't move on.

299
00:31:51.140 --> 00:31:53.140
They hold on to what I know.

300
00:31:53.140 --> 00:32:02.140
And even people who have moved on can have the temptation to go back and do things that way even now.

301
00:32:02.140 --> 00:32:11.140
And that's the thing in us that we find it extremely difficult to let go and to let go.

302
00:32:11.140 --> 00:32:15.140
So there's much more in this than we realize.

303
00:32:15.140 --> 00:32:22.140
So you will find therefore that in the divine will ministry it's all interior.

304
00:32:22.140 --> 00:32:24.140
It's not exterior.

305
00:32:24.140 --> 00:32:32.140
But the people at the other level will tell you, "Oh, but you should be doing this project and you should be doing that project and you should be involved in this.

306
00:32:32.140 --> 00:32:36.140
You should be involved in that. You should be involved in the other."

307
00:32:36.140 --> 00:32:40.140
We've been lifted up onto a different plane where all the work is interior.

308
00:32:40.140 --> 00:32:43.140
All of Louise's work was interior, wasn't it?

309
00:32:43.140 --> 00:32:49.140
What did she do externally apart from her embroidery? Nothing.

310
00:32:49.140 --> 00:32:54.140
She was called to the greatest so everything else had to go.

311
00:32:54.140 --> 00:32:57.140
Now we find that difficult to take on board.

312
00:32:57.140 --> 00:32:59.140
We understand it theoretically.

313
00:32:59.140 --> 00:33:01.140
But practically it's a different subject.

314
00:33:01.140 --> 00:33:08.140
So I want to leave that with you because that's a very important movement point.

315
00:33:08.140 --> 00:33:15.140
And Jesus said, "And yet who knew anything of what my mother was actually doing?"

316
00:33:15.140 --> 00:33:17.140
The answer is nobody.

317
00:33:17.140 --> 00:33:20.140
Only Jesus. And Joseph knew something.

318
00:33:20.140 --> 00:33:32.140
And yet what she did with the eternal one in order to obtain the great portant of the descent of the word into the midst of creatures.

319
00:33:32.140 --> 00:33:35.140
I mean, just look at what she actually did.

320
00:33:35.140 --> 00:33:44.140
It was known only that she was the cause of it by few at my conception.

321
00:33:44.140 --> 00:33:53.140
By many, when they saw me breathe my last on the cross, it was only when Jesus actually died on the cross and they declared him.

322
00:33:53.140 --> 00:34:01.140
It was his executioner who declared him a son of God that the divinity was actually seen.

323
00:34:01.140 --> 00:34:06.140
Now what was it on the cross that made people's eyes open?

324
00:34:06.140 --> 00:34:19.140
It was his humility, his patience, his kindness, his love, his concern for his neighbor, his massive forgiveness of his enemies.

325
00:34:19.140 --> 00:34:21.140
Everybody knew this is not human.

326
00:34:21.140 --> 00:34:25.140
This is not just, I should say, just human.

327
00:34:25.140 --> 00:34:27.140
This is not normal.

328
00:34:27.140 --> 00:34:36.140
And to die in complete surrender to God, complete love, complete forgiveness to everybody else, they said, "This one is a son of God.

329
00:34:36.140 --> 00:34:39.140
This is completely different."

330
00:34:39.140 --> 00:34:47.140
And so he said that it was only in his dying that they began to realize who he was.

331
00:34:47.140 --> 00:34:55.140
And yet some of them didn't see it, like the scribes and Pharisees didn't apparently see it.

332
00:34:55.140 --> 00:35:07.140
So my daughter Jesus said, "The greater the good that I want to do in the soul, and this good must descend for the good of the human generations

333
00:35:07.140 --> 00:35:13.140
and must bring me complete glory, the more I draw her to myself."

334
00:35:13.140 --> 00:35:20.140
Now the greater the mission that's given to you, the more the Lord wants to draw you to himself.

335
00:35:20.140 --> 00:35:28.140
And therefore for us living in the divine will, there's no way out of not being in union with God.

336
00:35:28.140 --> 00:35:32.140
The divine will thing means union with God.

337
00:35:32.140 --> 00:35:35.140
It has to be.

338
00:35:35.140 --> 00:35:42.140
And if you're living in union with God, you're living on a different sphere to everybody around you.

339
00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:59.140
So the more I draw her to myself and I make this good mature, this good, I make it mature and season between the soul and me.

340
00:35:59.140 --> 00:36:02.140
I segregate her from everybody.

341
00:36:02.140 --> 00:36:06.140
Oh dear, that's what he did with his blessed mother.

342
00:36:06.140 --> 00:36:08.140
That's what he did with Louisa.

343
00:36:08.140 --> 00:36:16.140
Now he can't do that completely with us because you're in a family and you're living a family life and so on.

344
00:36:16.140 --> 00:36:28.140
But in a sense he does because you'll find that the neighbors won't know what language you talk unless you find what language they talk and try to join them for a while.

345
00:36:28.140 --> 00:36:31.140
Otherwise you don't have a language in common.

346
00:36:31.140 --> 00:36:33.140
You don't have interest in common.

347
00:36:33.140 --> 00:36:34.140
You don't have a life in common.

348
00:36:34.140 --> 00:36:35.140
You don't have anything in common.

349
00:36:35.140 --> 00:36:43.140
So an actual factor segregated and therefore the people living at this level have a very great need for fellowship with each other.

350
00:36:43.140 --> 00:36:52.140
Have you noticed in order that you find someone at your own level and it becomes greater and greater.

351
00:36:52.140 --> 00:37:00.140
This needs to actually fellowship with somebody who actually understands the road you're on.

352
00:37:00.140 --> 00:37:05.140
I segregate her from everyone. I make her ignored. I love that one.

353
00:37:05.140 --> 00:37:06.140
I love that one.

354
00:37:06.140 --> 00:37:09.140
Notice the "I make her."

355
00:37:09.140 --> 00:37:13.140
That's the bit I would underline if it was me.

356
00:37:13.140 --> 00:37:21.140
I make, in other words, the Lord makes sure that you're isolated sufficiently for your safety.

357
00:37:21.140 --> 00:37:26.140
It's for your safety, your spiritual safety.

358
00:37:26.140 --> 00:37:32.140
Because if the others don't ignore you, they'll attack you.

359
00:37:32.140 --> 00:37:34.140
And you're not strong enough for that.

360
00:37:34.140 --> 00:37:37.140
You won't be able to do what he wants if you're being attacked all the time.

361
00:37:37.140 --> 00:37:39.140
I make her ignored.

362
00:37:39.140 --> 00:37:48.140
And when my will wants her to draw close to some other creature, it takes all my power in order for her to submit to the sacrifice.

363
00:37:48.140 --> 00:37:50.140
Now he's talking about Louisa.

364
00:37:50.140 --> 00:37:53.140
She doesn't want anybody visiting her and everything as you know.

365
00:37:53.140 --> 00:37:57.140
Therefore, let your Jesus do and calm yourself.

366
00:37:57.140 --> 00:37:59.140
Okay.

367
00:37:59.140 --> 00:38:10.140
Now, the next paragraph is a very important paragraph and it answers the question about people who doubt about living in the divine will.

368
00:38:10.140 --> 00:38:12.140
So just give yourself a heading.

369
00:38:12.140 --> 00:38:16.140
Answer to those who doubt about living in the divine will.

370
00:38:16.140 --> 00:38:17.140
And there are many.

371
00:38:17.140 --> 00:38:20.140
I don't know if you've met them.

372
00:38:20.140 --> 00:38:24.140
Okay.

373
00:38:24.140 --> 00:38:28.140
So Louisa said, my Jesus, they are right.

374
00:38:28.140 --> 00:38:34.140
They are the priests who are very doubtful about what Louisa is talking about.

375
00:38:34.140 --> 00:38:37.140
They say that they see no evidence.

376
00:38:37.140 --> 00:38:39.140
They see no positive good.

377
00:38:39.140 --> 00:38:41.140
And this is all just words.

378
00:38:41.140 --> 00:38:48.140
That's a most wonderful, wonderful statement because that is exactly what the unbelievers will say.

379
00:38:48.140 --> 00:38:51.140
It's all words.

380
00:38:51.140 --> 00:38:54.140
Or as they say in Ireland, it's all mouth.

381
00:38:54.140 --> 00:38:56.140
It's all just words.

382
00:38:56.140 --> 00:39:01.140
And she said, I don't really want anything.

383
00:39:01.140 --> 00:39:09.140
All I want is to do as you yourself want and that I do your most holy will.

384
00:39:09.140 --> 00:39:14.140
And that what passes between you and me remain as a secret in our hearts.

385
00:39:14.140 --> 00:39:17.140
Now that's not what he wants.

386
00:39:17.140 --> 00:39:22.140
She's saying, listen, I'm being badgered by these people who say this is all rubbish.

387
00:39:22.140 --> 00:39:25.140
And then I'm being badgered by you saying I have to do it.

388
00:39:25.140 --> 00:39:28.140
So I'm opting for your side.

389
00:39:28.140 --> 00:39:30.140
You know, can we just keep this quiet?

390
00:39:30.140 --> 00:39:32.140
Can we keep it secret?

391
00:39:32.140 --> 00:39:34.140
And Jesus said, am I a daughter?

392
00:39:34.140 --> 00:39:45.140
Would you like if I had worked my redemption in secret with my celestial father and my dear mother who was to conceive me?

393
00:39:45.140 --> 00:39:47.140
And nobody else would even know.

394
00:39:47.140 --> 00:39:52.140
Because if nobody knew where they're going to respond, no, it had to be proclaimed.

395
00:39:52.140 --> 00:39:57.140
Would we have acknowledged her immaculate conception if she hadn't told us?

396
00:39:57.140 --> 00:39:59.140
She had to tell us.

397
00:39:59.140 --> 00:40:01.140
She herself had to tell us.

398
00:40:01.140 --> 00:40:07.140
As great as a good might be, if it's not known, it does not produce life.

399
00:40:07.140 --> 00:40:08.140
It does not multiply.

400
00:40:08.140 --> 00:40:11.140
It's not loved and it's not imitated.

401
00:40:11.140 --> 00:40:13.140
You have to know.

402
00:40:13.140 --> 00:40:16.140
Listen, that's how the advertising works.

403
00:40:16.140 --> 00:40:22.140
That you dangle something in front of a person and you didn't know you wanted that thing until you saw it.

404
00:40:22.140 --> 00:40:33.140
You know, as I used to say in the past, I've been cured, thanks to God, that you'd walk past a shop and you'd see this magnificent blouse or something in the window.

405
00:40:33.140 --> 00:40:39.140
And all of a sudden you would have ten reasons for buying that, but you had none before you saw it.

406
00:40:39.140 --> 00:40:42.140
Do you know how to get cured of that?

407
00:40:42.140 --> 00:40:46.140
You'd walk past a shop and you'd say, "Thanks be to God, I need nothing."

408
00:40:46.140 --> 00:40:48.140
And I do that walking past it.

409
00:40:48.140 --> 00:40:50.140
I'm sure people think I'm mad.

410
00:40:50.140 --> 00:40:52.140
Thank you to God, I need nothing.

411
00:40:52.140 --> 00:40:53.140
I need nothing.

412
00:40:53.140 --> 00:40:54.140
I need nothing.

413
00:40:54.140 --> 00:40:55.140
And I'm blessing them all.

414
00:40:55.140 --> 00:40:56.140
I need nothing.

415
00:40:56.140 --> 00:41:00.140
And I walk out of a shopping center needing nothing.

416
00:41:00.140 --> 00:41:05.140
And sometimes I forget to buy what I went in for.

417
00:41:05.140 --> 00:41:12.140
Because I needed the exercise, you see, the exercise was getting free of the advertising.

418
00:41:12.140 --> 00:41:17.140
Getting free of what they put the nicest cake in the window, you see.

419
00:41:17.140 --> 00:41:18.140
Sorry?

420
00:41:18.140 --> 00:41:23.140
